head/.claude/scripts/lib/hop-locality.py:116 — HIGH: under `hounfour.locality: local_voices` a hop is "local" whenever its model or provider says `dispatch_group: local`; the endpoint host is never checked, so a declared provider with endpoint https://api.together.xyz/v1 labelled local is planned, dispatched to and recorded as local (reproduced with the head classifier). Same label-only rule at modelinv.py:476, openai_adapter.py:221 and Bridgebuilder config.ts:726 (which also ignores fallback_chain and admits CLI providers); nothing refuses the label at load.
head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py:541 — HIGH (same defect, inverse face; dissent DISS-C-001 confirmed): `_build_provider_config` reads `dispatch_group` from the model entry only, while hop-locality.py:116 and isLocalVoice honour a provider-block label; a hop planned and admitted as local therefore runs with no TransportPolicy (proxy env honoured, redirects followed) and MODELINV records it `hosted`.
head/.claude/skills/bridgebuilder-review/SKILL.md:117 — HIGH: claims providers/locality/exit follow the trusted source "even when the checkout is a PR head", but every voice dispatches through cheval, which loads the checkout's .loa.config.yaml; loadTrustedConfig (config.ts:602-700) refuses only head-only keyless/insecure flags, so a head that changes a trusted provider's endpoint or aliases is admitted and the prompt plus any {env:VAR} credential go where the head says.
